<title>FRANCE: Lagardere missiles unit wins NZ contract.</title>
<headline>Lagardere missiles unit wins NZ contract.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Matra BAe Dynamics, the missiles joint venture between Lagardere and British Aerospace Plc  BA., said on Thursday it has won a contract to supply the Matra Mistral air defence system to the New Zealand army.</p>
<p>The contract is for the tripod-launched version of the heat-seeking guided missile. No financial details were given.</p>
<p>New Zealand is the 20th country to order the Mistral system and is the first major government order from that country since France ended underground nuclear tests at the Muroroa atoll in the Pacific in January this year.</p>
</text>
